        "text": "The Scanner method nextByte() returns a byte value which can be stored in a byte variable.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "When concatenating a String with a byte, Java performs implicit casting (implicit type conversion) of the byte to a String.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "The Scanner method nextLine() adds a new line after the printed label because it reads the remainder of the line including the line separator.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "If a floating‑point number (e.g., 20.1) is entered when using nextInt(), a runtime exception occurs because the method can only parse integer values.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "To read a floating‑point number with Scanner, use nextFloat() or nextDouble() instead of nextInt().",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Scanner.next() returns the next token (a sequence of characters up to whitespace).",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Scanner.nextLine() reads the remainder of the current line, including spaces, whereas Scanner.next() reads only up to the next whitespace.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "When reading a full name with spaces using Scanner, calling next() once returns only the first token; a second call to next() is needed to obtain the second token.",
        "refs": ["Q0004", "Q0005"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
